  "doctrine": [],
  "note": "Anaharath (Joshua 19:19) is a town of Issachar. The boundary list offers no evidence that its name means groaning. The pronoun נַחְנוּ belongs with אֲנַחְנוּ. The Arabic comparison points to ḥ. The alternative reconstruction with ḫ depends on a proposed connection with Akkadian weariness."
